  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Financial Sector Stability and Reforms Program (Subprogram 1)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program adopts a programmatic policy-based loan (PBL) modality with two subprograms of $200 million each to properly sequence reforms and ensure the needed flexibility while implementing multi-year policy reforms in a crisis period. Subprogram 1 prioritizes immediate reforms to enhance the crisis management regulatory framework and stabilizing the financial sector while subprogram 2 prioritizes follow-on reforms to build a resilient and inclusive financial system. It will be supported by an attached transaction technical assistance (TA) for subprogram 2 and post-program partnership framework (PPPF) activities. A programmatic approach that combines policy-based loans, TA, and knowledge support was selected as it allows complex and challenging reforms to be addressed comprehensively.</narrative>
  </description>
